Done. Both files are now consistent:

**`sifli_start.c`** — uses CMSIS types from `cmsis_gcc.h`:
```c
#include "cmsis_gcc.h"

for (__copy_table_t const *pTable = &__copy_table_start__;
     pTable < &__copy_table_end__; ++pTable) {
    for (uint32_t i = 0u; i < pTable->wlen; ++i)
        pTable->dest[i] = pTable->src[i];
}

for (__zero_table_t const *pTable = &__zero_table_start__;
     pTable < &__zero_table_end__; ++pTable) {
    for (uint32_t i = 0u; i < pTable->wlen; ++i)
        pTable->dest[i] = 0u;
}
```

**`ld.script`** — stores word count (`SIZEOF / 4`):
```ld
LONG (SIZEOF(.data) / 4)        /* .data word count */
LONG (SIZEOF(.retm_data) / 4)   /* .retm_data word count */
LONG ((__bss_end__ - __bss_start__) / 4)  /* .bss word count */
LONG (SIZEOF(.retm_bss) / 4)    /* .retm_bss word count */
```

CMSIS struct layout:
- `__copy_table_t` = `{uint32_t const *src, uint32_t *dest, uint32_t wlen}` — 12 bytes
- `__zero_table_t` = `{uint32_t *dest, uint32_t wlen}` — 8 bytes
